## Why This Is Asked
Addresses multi-source schema drift and basic data unification, a common beginner challenge.

## Key Concepts
- Schema unification across sources
- Type coercion rules and compatibility
- Parquet partitioning and Glue Catalog
- Simple schema versioning and data quality checks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: unify two schemas into canonical and write Parquet
function merge(a,b){
  const canon = {};
  // map fields, coerce types
  canon.id = toIntOrNull(a.id||b.id);
  canon.name = a.name||b.name;
  // nested fields example
  canon.meta = a.meta ?? b.meta ?? {};
  return canon;
}
```

